__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.env
*.log
node_modules/
# Worktrees the review subagent runs in (isolation: "worktree"). Ignored
# in the bridge since Cycle 108 and not here, which left them one
# `git add -A` away from being committed by the cycle under review.
.claude/

# Scratch from the digest roll in `prompt.md` step 7, which tells a cycle
# to `cd` into this repo and write `live.md`/`archive.md` here before
# calling `tools.roll_digest`. They are fragments of Edvard's
# `journal-digest.md`, not source, and they have been swept into a commit
# by `git add -A` twice: Cycle 125 caught it before merging, Cycle 132
# did not, and #111 shipped both files to `main`. Ignoring them is the
# only version of this fix that does not depend on the next cycle
# remembering.
/live.md
/live2.md
/archive.md

# Every other scratch file `prompt.md` tells a cycle to write into this
# repo root -- and the enumerated list that used to live here is gone,
# because enumerating was the bug. It was extended three times (the digest
# roll's three, then `claims.json`/`ledger.json`, then `iss.md`) and each
# time it was extended by a cycle cleaning up a file that had *already*
# been committed. It still did not have `prompt.md`, `prompt-cur.md`,
# `live-new.md`, `entry.md`, `entry2.md` or `newsections.md` in it, and
# the first three of those were tracked on `main` until Cycle 220.
#
# `prompt.md` is the one that did damage rather than just sitting there:
# it is a stale copy of Nova's own constitution, and Cycle 220's review
# subagent grepped it instead of the live one in the vault, found no
# mention of the change under review, and returned a confident finding
# that the fix had never been wired in. It had been -- in the vault, which
# is the only place any of those three documents really live.
#
# So the rule is inverted. Nothing at this repo root is a `.md` or a
# `.json` except the three named below; everything else there is a cycle's
# scratch by construction, including the ones nobody has invented yet.
# `tests/test_repo_root_is_clean.py` fails loudly if one is committed
# anyway, since an ignore rule does nothing to a file already tracked.
/*.md
!/README.md
/*.json
!/package.json
!/tsconfig.json
